<body style="height: auto; min-height: auto;">Ref No: {{{Case.Case_Number__c}}}<br />
<br />
Hi {{{Case.First_Name__c}}},&nbsp;<br />
&nbsp;<br />
Thank you for contacting Qantas Customer Care regarding your disrupted journey from {{{Case.Departure_City__c}}} on {{{Case.Email_Departure_Date_Time__c}}}.<br />
<br />
I appreciate how inconvenient this delay was for you and was sorry to learn about the impact it had on your plans in {{{Case.Arrival_City__c}}}.<br />
<br />
<strong>Things don’t always go to plan</strong><br />
<br />
We’re committed to getting you to your destination on time, however, bad weather, natural disasters, technical problems and other issues can cause flight delays and cancellations, and your safety is our first priority.<br />
<br />
Though this delay was out of our control, I can understand how frustrating it must have been.<br />
<br />
<em><strong>-If requesting compensation add:-</strong></em><br />
<br />
<strong>We’re here to help</strong><br />
<br />
I'm sorry to hear that the delay meant you missed your &lt;event/meeting/dinner/concert/planned accommodation/train&gt;.<br />
<br />
While we can’t provide compensation on this occasion, if you had any unexpected expenses because of the &lt;delay/cancellation&gt;, your travel insurance policy may cover these sorts of situations.<br />
<br />
Please let us know if you’d like us to provide you with an insurance letter to assist with any claim.<br />
<br />
<strong>We value your opinion</strong><br />
<br />
Customer feedback plays an important role in our continuous improvement process so that we can provide you with exceptional service from start to finish.<br />
<br />
Thank you for taking the time to let us know about your experience and we look forward to welcoming you onboard again soon.<br />
<br />
&nbsp;</body>
